{{!-- components/nav-icon.hbs — maps a navigation item's slug to an icon.
     Param: slug. An unknown slug renders NOTHING, which is the point: a
     publisher can add any menu item in Ghost Admin and it simply appears
     without an icon rather than with a wrong one.

     Independent {{#match}} blocks, not an {{else match}} chain: every slug is
     tested, exactly one can win, and adding a row can never break the row
     above it. Icon names are the canonical ones from partials/icons.hbs —
     several slugs deliberately share a glyph (docs/documentation,
     training/roadmaps), because they are the same destination by two names. --}}
{{#match slug "home"}}{{> icons name="house" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{/match}}
{{#match slug "courses"}}{{> icons name="graduation-cap" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{/match}}
{{#match slug "training"}}{{> icons name="steps" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{/match}}
{{#match slug "roadmaps"}}{{> icons name="map-trifold" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{/match}}
{{#match slug "blog"}}{{> icons name="article" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{/match}}
